# A commit message is published exactly as typed and cannot be edited after a push, so it
# gets the same name check the export path has always had. Labels only — see
# buzz-agents/scripts/check-text-for-names.mjs.
#
# --commit-msg is what makes the `#` exemption apply. A commit message is the only input
# where a `#` line is discarded before publication, so it is the only one that gets it —
# everywhere else, a comment is prose and is read. Do not drop this flag, and do not add it
# to any other caller.
node buzz-agents/scripts/check-text-for-names.mjs --commit-msg "$1"
